R"VG(
# modern3.vg (H-04, the second pass): the weather on the air: the forecast (a reel or a disc) and the bulletin's weather. The world's own
# weather by its season and climate, over its own land (its traits: the canyons, the salt flats, the lake country), its sky (its moons,
# its ring, its lights), with advice for that people's herds, boats and fields and a saying of theirs now and then.

genre.weather (words=22..62)
  {wx.open} {wx.line} {wx.line} {wx.line} {wx.close}
  {wx.open} {wx.line} {wx.line} {wx.sky} {wx.close}
  {wx.open} {wx.line} {wx.advice} {wx.line} {wx.close}
  {wx.open} {wx.line} {wx.line} {wx.outlook} {wx.close}
  {wx.open} {wx.line} {wx.temp} {wx.advice} {wx.close}

wx.open (formula people=3)
  And now the weather, for {season.now}.
  Here is the forecast for tonight and tomorrow.
  The weather, from the station at {$seat}.
  Now the forecast for the land and the coasts.
  Here is the weather.
  And the outlook for the next day and night.
  The weather service, with the forecast.
wx.close (formula people=3)
  That is the weather.
  More at the hour.
  That was the forecast.
  The next forecast is at dawn.
  And that is the weather for {season.now}.
  Dress for it.

# ---- a line of the forecast: where, what, and how it goes ----------------------------------------------------------------------

wx.line
  {wx.region}, {wx.cond}, {wx.then}.
  {wx.region}: {wx.cond}, {wx.then}.
  {wx.cond} {wx.region2}, {wx.then}.
  Expect {wx.cond} {wx.region2}, {wx.then}.
  {wx.region}, {wx.cond}; {wx.cond2} later.
  {wx.region2b} there will be {wx.cond}, {wx.then}.

wx.region
  In the north
  In the south
  In the east
  In the west
  Inland
  Over {land}
  Around {mountain}
  In {$seat}
  Round {$home}
  On the high ground
  In the hill towns
  (coast=1) Along the coast
  (coast=1) Out at sea
  (desert=0) In the river valleys
  (archipelago=1) On the islands
  (lakeland=1) Across the lake country
  (canyons=1) In the canyons
  (saltflats=1) Over the salt flats
  (erg=1) Over the sand sea
  (geysers=1) By the hot springs
  (economy=farming|economy2=farming) Across the farm country
wx.region2
  in the north
  in the south
  over {land}
  around {mountain}
  in {$seat}
  on the high ground
  inland
  (coast=1) along the coast
  (desert=0) in the valleys
  (archipelago=1) over the islands
  (lakeland=1) over the lakes
wx.region2b
  In the north
  Inland
  Over {land}
  On the high ground
  (coast=1) Along the coast
  Around {mountain}

wx.cond
  (2) {weather.now}
  clear skies
  bright spells
  cloud building from the west
  a gusty wind
  (desert=0) showers, some of them heavy
  (desert=0) low cloud and drizzle
  (desert=0) fog at first
  (desert=0 seasons=4 season=3) a hard frost
  (desert=0 seasons=4 season=3 cold=1) snow on the high ground
  (desert=0 seasons=4 season=0) a cold wind and bright spells
  (desert=0 seasons=4 season=1) a close, heavy heat
  (seasons=4 season=1) thunder in the afternoon
  (desert=0 seasons=4 season=2) gales
  (desert=0 seasons=4 season=2) rain in long bands
  (desert=0 seasons=2 season=0) rain, and more rain
  (desert=0 seasons=2 season=1) dry heat
  (desert=1) dust in the air
  (desert=1) a dry wind off the dunes
  (desert=1) a cold, clear night
  (desert=1 season=1) fierce heat
  (coast=1) a wind off the sea
  (coast=1 desert=0) sea mist
  (haze=1) the haze, thicker than usual
  (storms=1) storms, as ever
  (cold=1) a bitter wind
wx.cond2
  clearer skies
  heavier rain
  a dropping wind
  a colder wind
  sunshine for a while
  (desert=1) a dust haze
  (desert=0) more showers
wx.then
  clearing by morning
  easing later
  turning colder after dark
  with more to come
  dying out by evening
  much as today
  heavier towards dawn
  lifting by noon
  spreading east overnight
  slow to clear
  on and off all day
  with no change in sight
  brighter later
  worse before it is better

wx.temp
  {wx.region}, {wx.feel}.
  It will be {wx.feel2} {wx.region2} tonight.
wx.feel
  a cold night, with frost in the hollows
  warm for the time of year
  cooler than of late
  mild, and damp with it
  the warmest night of {season.now} so far
  close and sticky
wx.feel2
  cold
  warm
  close
  bitter
  mild

# ---- the sky, the advice, the outlook --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

wx.sky
  (moons>0 coast=1) {moon} is full tonight; the tides will be high.
  (moons>0) {moon} rises late; a dark night for the stars.
  (moons=2) Both moons are up after midnight, if the cloud allows.
  (moons>2) All the moons are up after midnight, if the cloud allows.
  (rings=1) The ring will be clear in the south after dark.
  (rings=1) The ring's shadow crosses the north at noon; it will be dim for an hour.
  (aurora=1) The lights may be seen in the north tonight.
  (comet=1) The hairy star is low in the west before dawn.
  (companion=1) The second sun sets an hour after the first tonight.
  (glowflora=1) A still, dark night; the woods will glow.
  (locked=1) The edge of the day moves a little further this week, the observatory says.
  The stars will be out over {mountain} after midnight.
  {skynight} will be bright enough to read by, if anyone wants to.

wx.advice (share=0.6)
  (economy=herding|economy2=herding) Herders on the high ground should bring the {herd} down.
  (economy=farming|economy2=farming) Gardeners should cover the {veg} tonight.
  (coast=1) Fishing boats are advised to stay in harbour.
  Drivers should take care on the hill roads.
  It will be a night for {drink} and an early bed.
  Anyone hanging out washing should think again.
  Keep the {herd} in if you can.
  The old people say {proverb}; tonight they may be right.
  Bring in anything made of {material} that you mind about.
  The ferries may not run in the morning.
  Schools will open late if the roads are bad.
  Keep {fuel} by the door; the night will be long.

wx.outlook
  Looking further ahead: {wx.cond} at first, then {wx.cond2}.
  The outlook for {season.next}: {wx.out}.
  For the rest of the week, {wx.cond}, {wx.then}.
wx.out
  more of the same
  drier than usual
  wetter than usual
  colder, and early
  no better, and possibly worse
  the forecasters will not say

# ---- the bulletin's weather (modern.vg) -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

bc.weather
  The weather: {wx.cond} {wx.region2} tonight, {wx.then}.
  And the weather for {season.now}: {wx.cond}, {wx.then}.
  Finally, the weather: {wx.region}, {wx.cond}; {wx.region2}, {wx.cond2}.
  The weather tomorrow: {wx.cond}, {wx.then}. {wx.sky}
  Tonight's weather: {wx.cond} {wx.region2}; tomorrow, {wx.cond2}.
)VG"
